      "id": "fold-rail",
      "kind": "step-rail",
      "presentation": "Place below the explanation, above the experiment. Use state short labels. Keep progress and trace exclusively in this rail.",
      "bind": {
        "active": "state.id",
        "items": "variant.states"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cross-validation-picture",
      "kind": "fixed-picture",
      "presentation": "Use the canonical algorithm/collection arrangement within the approved shell. Arrange folds in one row and models below. Keep region positions fixed. During fold states, highlighted folds are held out; unhighlighted folds supply training examples. Setup highlights nothing; comparison highlights both models. Bind all visible labels and contents to regions. Reserve readable label space at native width.",
      "bind": {
        "active": "state.active",
        "links": "variant.links",
        "regions": "variant.regions"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "error-comparison",
      "kind": "value-readout",
      "presentation": "Use two columns, one per model, with training above held-out results. Fold values show incorrect predictions divided by evaluated examples. Summary values are percentages computed from those same counts. Average training rates across fits; pool held-out counts across folds. Equal fold sizes make pooled held-out error equal mean fold error. All percentages are exact; no rounding is required. Keep numerical results here, not in callouts.",
      "bind": {
        "values": "state.readouts"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "active-explanation",
      "kind": "active-callout",
      "presentation": "Anchor to the named region without covering labels. Use the sentence as the bound status line and the reason as mechanism explanation. Identify where evidence comes from without repeating numerical results.",
